---
import { Container } from '@components/odyssey-theme';
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Page.astro';

const seo = {
	title: 'SML | tevsys',
	description:
		'SML (Smart Money Lock): optional bonus from yesterday’s profit to widen your allowed margin — only with your click. Validation in progress with evidence on profit and widened-loss closes (Advanced/Pro).',
};
---

<Layout seo={seo} lang="en">
	<div class="tevsys-feature-micro-surface tevsys-feature-micro-surface--sml">
	<Container>
		<section class="feature-hero">
			<p class="feature-kicker">Discipline feature</p>
			<h1>SML: <span class="feature-title__accent">protect</span> part of what you earned without freezing your trading.</h1>
			<p class="feature-hook"><span class="feature-hook__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Turn it on when you want. Choose how much to widen the margin: from <span class="feature-hook__accent">5%</span> to <span class="feature-hook__accent">25%</span> (at least <span class="feature-hook__accent">75%</span> stays protected).</p>
			<p class="feature-lead">
				<span class="feature-title__accent">Optional and under your control</span>: it sits alongside daily and weekly limits; you only widen the margin when you activate the bonus calculated from yesterday’s profit.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section id="sml-panel" class="feature-demo feature-demo--hero">
			<div class="sml-multichart">
				<p class="feature-hook sml-multichart__lead">
					<span class="feature-hook__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					<span>One chart for tevsys. Your whole account, protected.</span>
				</p>
				<p class="sml-multichart__sub">Protection notices show on every open chart.</p>
			</div>
			<h2>How it looks on the panel today</h2>
			<p class="feature-demo-hook">
				Yesterday’s profit &gt; threshold · optional bonus · <strong class="feature-title__accent">SML DISPONIBLE</strong> and <strong class="feature-title__accent">SML 1‑CLICK</strong> on the panel.
			</p>
			<figure class="sml-panel-embed">
				<a
					class="proof-gallery__zoom"
					href="/images/evidence/sml-panel-validacion-demo.png?v=20260830b"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					aria-label="Open full-size SML panel screenshot"
				>
					<img
						class="proof-gallery__image"
						src="/images/evidence/sml-panel-validacion-demo.png?v=20260830b"
						width="520"
						height="780"
						loading="lazy"
						decoding="async"
						alt="tevsys panel on chart: active limits, SML DISPONIBLE and SML 1-CLICK in teal, NOTICIAS and HORARIOS OFF."
					/>
				</a>
			</figure>
			<p class="demo-edit-note">
				<strong>Demo</strong> ActivTrades account (Aug 2026). Current panel (SML in teal) on the chart. Click to enlarge. Not advice or a promise of results. On-screen EA UI may still appear in Spanish.
			</p>
		</section>

		<p class="sml-validation-banner" role="note">
			<strong>Advanced/Pro · validation in progress.</strong> Not available on Essential. This page shows progress we can already demonstrate — not a full catalogue. <strong>Only what the build proves</strong> in the terminal.
		</p>

		<section class="feature-proof">
			<h2>What you can verify</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><a class="evidence-link" href="#sml-panel">SML panel: bonus available before you activate (demo capture).</a></li>
				<li><a class="evidence-link" href="#sml-evidence">Scenarios documented so far (profit, widened loss, coexistence with limits).</a></li>
				<li><a class="evidence-link" href="#sml-perdida-ampliada">Validated close on widened loss (live account, May 2026).</a></li>
				<li><a class="evidence-link" href="#sml-demo-flow">Step-by-step demo flow — activation, close, and SML ON.</a></li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section id="sml-evidence" class="feature-proof-detail">
			<h3>What we can show today</h3>
			<p class="feature-proof-subtitle">Documented progress — not a closed catalogue</p>
			<ul class="sml-checklist">
				<li><strong>Close with SML in profit:</strong> stable flow with active bonus and stop at the agreed limit — checked against panel, MT5 report, and internal traces.</li>
				<li><strong>Close with SML on widened loss:</strong> the day’s loss margin widens only with SML on; protection fires past that widened ceiling, not at the base limit without bonus.</li>
				<li><strong>Same account, same rules:</strong> coexists with daily limits, weekly limits, and OFF days without mixed on-screen messages.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section id="sml-perdida-ampliada" class="feature-proof-detail">
			<h3>Validated on a widened-loss close</h3>
			<p class="feature-proof-subtitle">Live account · May 2026</p>
			<p class="feature-proof-lead">
				Daily loss with widened margin — <strong>STOP · SML ON</strong> · limits <strong class="feature-title__accent">−0.75% → −0.78%</strong> · <strong>SML widened</strong> and account protected until end of session.
			</p>
			<p class="proof-gallery__hint">Click the capture to enlarge it.</p>
			<figure class="sml-capture-embed">
				<a
					class="proof-gallery__zoom"
					href="/images/evidence/sml-cierre-perdida-ampliada-validado.png"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					aria-label="Open full-size panel capture after SML widened-loss close"
				>
					<img
						class="proof-gallery__image"
						src="/images/evidence/sml-cierre-perdida-ampliada-validado.png"
						width="314"
						height="445"
						loading="lazy"
						decoding="async"
						alt="tevsys panel after close: STOP for daily loss with SML active, TODAY limits -0.75% to -0.78%, SML widened and protected until end of day."
					/>
				</a>
				<figcaption class="sml-capture-caption">
					Panel only — no chart noise. State after the automatic close.
				</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<p class="sml-proof-note">
				<strong>Why don’t the STOP percent and the day result match to the cent?</strong> The system cuts when it hits the <strong>widened ceiling</strong> in live market; the day’s result can land a tick under or over — same pattern as other documented tevsys closes.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section id="sml-demo-flow" class="feature-proof-detail">
			<h3>In demo: activation, close, and SML state</h3>
			<p class="feature-proof-subtitle">Three moments of the same flow (prior validation)</p>
			<p class="feature-proof-lead">
				See the widened limit before you apply it, the result at close, and the panel with <strong>SML active</strong> after protection.
			</p>
			<details id="sml-demo-flow-evidence" class="proof-accordion">
				<summary class="proof-capture-link">Step-by-step captures — activation, close, and SML ON</summary>
				<p class="proof-gallery__hint">Click each capture to view it full size.</p>
				<div class="sml-proof-grid">
					<figure class="sml-proof-card">
						<a
							class="proof-gallery__zoom"
							href="/images/evidence/sml-481-step-01-activacion.png"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
							aria-label="Open full-size step 1 SML activation capture"
						>
							<img
								class="proof-gallery__image"
								src="/images/evidence/sml-481-step-01-activacion.png"
								width="905"
								height="809"
								alt="Before activating SML: confirmation modal and panel with widened limit visible."
								loading="lazy"
								decoding="async"
							/>
						</a>
						<figcaption><strong>Step 1 — Activation:</strong> widened limit visible before applying the bonus.</figcaption>
					</figure>
					<figure class="sml-proof-card">
						<a
							class="proof-gallery__zoom"
							href="/images/evidence/sml-481-step-02-cierre.png"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
							aria-label="Open full-size step 2 SML close capture"
						>
							<img
								class="proof-gallery__image"
								src="/images/evidence/sml-481-step-02-cierre.png"
								width="424"
								height="599"
								alt="Final result with SML active after the widened-loss close."
								loading="lazy"
								decoding="async"
							/>
						</a>
						<figcaption><strong>Step 2 — Close:</strong> day result after firing at the widened ceiling.</figcaption>
					</figure>
					<figure class="sml-proof-card">
						<a
							class="proof-gallery__zoom"
							href="/images/evidence/sml-481-step-03-estado-sml-on.png"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
							aria-label="Open full-size step 3 SML ON state capture"
						>
							<img
								class="proof-gallery__image"
								src="/images/evidence/sml-481-step-03-estado-sml-on.png"
								width="860"
								height="738"
								alt="Panel with SML active and protection until end of session after the close."
								loading="lazy"
								decoding="async"
							/>
						</a>
						<figcaption><strong>Step 3 — SML ON state:</strong> account protected until end of session.</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
			</details>
			<p class="sml-proof-note sml-proof-note--slim">
				In demo, the widened ceiling and the final close can differ slightly (same pattern as other live-market tevsys closes).
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="feature-cta">
			<h2>Want to validate SML for Advanced/Pro?</h2>
			<p>We’ll show validation status and the scenarios you can check against your real limits (Advanced/Pro, waitlist).</p>
			<a href="/en/company/contact?feature=sml&flow=demo" class="feature-cta__button">Request SML review</a>
		</section>
	</Container>
	</div>
</Layout>

<script>
	const openDemoFlowIfTarget = () => {
		const hash = window.location.hash;
		if (hash === '#sml-demo-flow' || hash === '#sml-demo-flow-evidence') {
			const details = document.getElementById('sml-demo-flow-evidence');
			if (details && !details.open) details.open = true;
		}
	};
	openDemoFlowIfTarget();
	window.addEventListener('hashchange', openDemoFlowIfTarget);
</script>

<style>
	.feature-hero,
	.feature-demo,
	.feature-proof,
	.feature-proof-detail,
	.feature-cta {
		margin: var(--section-margin) auto;
	}
	.feature-kicker {
		margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
		opacity: 0.8;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		font-size: 0.82rem;
	}
	.feature-title__accent {
		color: #f5b041;
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.feature-hook {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		font-style: italic;
		font-weight: 600;
		opacity: 0.9;
		margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}
	.feature-hook__dot {
		width: 0.45rem;
		height: 0.45rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: #f5b041;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}
	.feature-hook__accent {
		color: #f5b041;
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.feature-lead {
		max-width: 70ch;
		line-height: 1.55;
	}
	.feature-demo--hero {
		position: relative;
	}
	.feature-demo--hero::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		inset: -0.35rem;
		border-radius: calc(var(--feature-micro-radius, clamp(0.85rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem)) + 2px);
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.18), rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.04));
		pointer-events: none;
		z-index: 0;
	}
	/* Hero panel: acabado global (--micro-demo-bg); sin halo ::before */
	#sml-panel.feature-demo--hero::before {
		display: none;
	}
	.feature-demo--hero > * {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
	}
	.sml-multichart {
		margin: 0 0 clamp(1rem, 2.8vw, 1.5rem);
		max-width: 52ch;
		padding-bottom: clamp(0.6rem, 1.8vw, 0.85rem);
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07);
	}
	html[data-theme='light'] .sml-multichart {
		border-bottom-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
	}
	.sml-multichart__lead {
		margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: 0.4rem;
		font-size: clamp(0.92rem, 2.1vw, 0.98rem);
		font-style: normal;
		font-weight: 500;
		opacity: 0.82;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}
	.sml-multichart__lead .feature-hook__dot {
		margin-top: 0.32rem;
		width: 0.35rem;
		height: 0.35rem;
		opacity: 0.85;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}
	.sml-multichart__sub {
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: calc(0.35rem + 0.4rem);
		font-size: clamp(0.8rem, 1.85vw, 0.86rem);
		font-style: normal;
		font-weight: 400;
		opacity: 0.62;
		line-height: 1.5;
		letter-spacing: 0.01em;
	}
	html[data-theme='light'] .sml-multichart__sub {
		opacity: 0.68;
	}
	.feature-demo h2,
	.feature-proof h2,
	.feature-cta h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
		font-size: 1.35rem;
	}
	.feature-demo-hook {
		margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
		max-width: 58ch;
		line-height: 1.5;
		font-size: 0.96rem;
		opacity: 0.92;
	}
	.sml-panel-embed,
	.sml-capture-embed {
		margin: 0 auto 0.75rem;
		max-width: min(100%, 28rem);
	}
	.sml-capture-embed {
		max-width: min(100%, 20rem);
	}
	.sml-panel-embed .proof-gallery__zoom,
	.sml-capture-embed .proof-gallery__zoom {
		border-radius: var(--feature-micro-radius, clamp(0.85rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem));
		overflow: hidden;
		border: 1px solid rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.35);
		box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
	}
	.sml-panel-embed .proof-gallery__zoom {
		max-width: min(100%, 18rem);
		margin-inline: auto;
	}
	.sml-capture-embed .proof-gallery__zoom {
		margin-inline: auto;
	}
	.demo-edit-note {
		margin: 0 auto;
		max-width: 58ch;
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		opacity: 0.82;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}
	.sml-capture-caption {
		margin-top: 0.55rem;
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
		opacity: 0.78;
		text-align: center;
		max-width: 36ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
	}
	.sml-validation-banner {
		margin: calc(var(--section-margin) * 0.5) auto calc(var(--section-margin) * 0.85);
		max-width: 74ch;
		padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		font-size: 0.94rem;
		border-radius: var(--feature-micro-radius, clamp(0.85rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem));
		border: 1px solid rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.32);
		background: rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.07);
	}
	.feature-proof {
		position: relative;
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.feature-proof::after {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		top: 0;
		right: -10%;
		width: 42%;
		height: 100%;
		pointer-events: none;
		background: radial-gradient(ellipse at right center, rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.11) 0%, rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.045) 42%, transparent 74%);
	}
	.feature-proof ul {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.feature-proof li {
		margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		padding: 0.42rem 0.6rem 0.42rem 1rem;
		border-left: 2px solid rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.22);
		border-radius: 0.35rem;
		background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.025), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0));
		transition: border-color 0.2s ease, background-color 0.2s ease;
	}
	.feature-proof li::before {
		content: '';
		display: inline-block;
		width: 0.34rem;
		height: 0.34rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.82);
		margin-right: 0.55rem;
		vertical-align: middle;
	}
	.feature-proof li:hover {
		border-left-color: rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.42);
		background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.07), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0));
	}
	.feature-proof li:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	.evidence-link {
		color: #ffffff;
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-decoration-thickness: 0.06em;
		text-underline-offset: 2.5px;
		transition: color 0.2s ease;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.evidence-link:hover {
		color: #f5b041;
	}
	.evidence-link:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px solid #f5b041;
		outline-offset: 3px;
		border-radius: 0.2rem;
	}
	.feature-proof-detail {
		border-radius: var(--feature-micro-radius, clamp(0.85rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem));
		padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
		scroll-margin-top: 5.5rem;
		transition: border-color 0.25s ease, background-color 0.25s ease;
	}
	.feature-proof-detail h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.45rem;
	}
	.feature-proof-detail h3::before {
		content: '';
		width: 0.42rem;
		height: 0.42rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: #f5b041;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}
	.feature-proof-subtitle {
		margin: -0.1rem 0 0.5rem !important;
		font-size: 0.94rem;
		font-style: italic;
		font-weight: 600;
		opacity: 0.9;
	}
	.feature-proof-lead {
		margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
		font-size: 0.94rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		opacity: 0.88;
		max-width: 52ch;
	}
	#sml-panel:target {
		border-color: rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.42);
		background: linear-gradient(148deg, rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.06), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02));
		box-shadow: none;
	}
	.sml-checklist {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.sml-checklist li {
		margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		padding: 0.42rem 0.6rem 0.42rem 1rem;
		border-left: 2px solid rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.22);
		border-radius: 0.35rem;
		background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.025), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0));
	}
	.sml-checklist li::before {
		content: '';
		display: inline-block;
		width: 0.34rem;
		height: 0.34rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.82);
		margin-right: 0.55rem;
		vertical-align: middle;
	}
	.sml-checklist li:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	.proof-gallery__hint {
		margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		opacity: 0.82;
		line-height: 1.45;
		max-width: 68ch;
	}
	.proof-gallery__zoom {
		display: block;
		cursor: zoom-in;
	}
	.proof-gallery__zoom:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px solid #f5b041;
		outline-offset: 3px;
	}
	.proof-gallery__image {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}
	.proof-accordion {
		margin-top: 0.35rem;
	}
	.proof-accordion summary {
		list-style: none;
	}
	.proof-accordion summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}
	.proof-capture-link {
		color: #f5b041;
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.proof-capture-link:hover {
		color: #f7c050;
	}
	.sml-proof-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 0.9rem;
		margin-top: 0.65rem;
	}
	.sml-proof-card {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0.7rem;
		border-radius: var(--feature-micro-radius, clamp(0.85rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem));
	}
	.sml-proof-card .proof-gallery__zoom {
		border-radius: calc(var(--feature-micro-radius, clamp(0.85rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem)) - 0.15rem);
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.sml-proof-card img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}
	.sml-proof-card figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.55rem;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
		opacity: 0.9;
	}
	.sml-proof-note {
		margin: 0.95rem 0 0;
		padding: 0.8rem 0.95rem;
		border-radius: var(--feature-micro-radius, clamp(0.85rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem));
		border: 1px solid rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.28);
		background: rgba(245, 176, 65, 0.06);
		line-height: 1.5;
		font-size: 0.94rem;
	}
	.sml-proof-note--slim {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
	}
	#sml-panel,
	#sml-evidence,
	#sml-perdida-ampliada,
	#sml-demo-flow {
		scroll-margin-top: 5.5rem;
	}
	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		.sml-proof-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
